  "body": {
    "id": "prop:edgeless-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "If \\(G_n\\) is edgeless, then \\(D_n=\\lambda_n=1\\), every \\(B_{n,i}=\\varnothing\\), and \\(q_{n,i}=1/4\\). The fixed \\(r=2\\) CGD estimator is therefore a sum of independent modified Horvitz--Thompson endpoint contrasts, and \\(K_n(1;B,c)\\to0\\), recovering the classical independent triangular-array central limit theorem under the stated fourth moments and variance floor.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "G_n",
      "D_n",
      "\\lambda_n",
      "B_{n,i}",
      "q_{n,i}",
      "i",
      "T_n",
      "K_n(d;B,c)",
      "n",
      "B",
      "c"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:cgd-estimator",
      "thm:uniform-normal-bound",
      "def:desired-coordinate-design"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "If \\(G_n\\) is edgeless, every degree is zero, so \\(D_n=1\\), \\(A_{G_n}=0\\), and \\(\\lambda_n=1\\).  The definition of earlier neighbors gives \\(B_{n,i}=\\varnothing\\), and \\(\\mathrm{def:desired\\text{-}coordinate\\text{-}design}\\) gives \\(q_{n,i}=1/4\\).  Thus the centered raw estimator is the sum of the independent centered variables\n\\[\n X_{n,i}=4\\{a_{n,i}\\mathbf1(U_{n,i}=1)-b_{n,i}\\mathbf1(U_{n,i}=0)\\}-(a_{n,i}-b_{n,i}).\n\\]\nTheir aggregate fourth moment is bounded by \\(CBn\\), whereas the variance floor gives \\(\\operatorname{Var}_U(\\sum_iX_{n,i})=n^2\\sigma_n^2\\ge cn\\); this is the usual uniform Lyapunov condition.  Equivalently, substituting \\(D_n=\\lambda_n=1\\) into \\(\\mathrm{thm:uniform\\text{-}normal\\text{-}bound}\\) gives\n\\[\n K_n(1;B,c)\\le C_{\\mathrm N}(B,c)(2/n)^{1/5}\\longrightarrow0.\n\\]\nThis is precisely the corrected degree envelope at \\(D_n=1\\), with the factor \\(2\\) retained inside the fifth root.  It proves the stated independent-design reduction and its central limit conclusion.",
    "justification": "The reduction is the required sanity check at the no-interference boundary.",
    "gap": "This is a consistency check against classical Berry--Esseen theory rather than a novelty claim.",
    "consumer": "It verifies that the frontier does not distort ordinary independent randomization inference.",
